 176	
 177	`type` is `"bar" | "line"`; `value` is numeric. Display only.
 178	
 179	#### `interactive_plot`
 180	
 181	```json
 182	{
 183	  "id": "decay-lab",
 184	  "kind": "interactive_plot",
 185	  "props": {
 186	    "title": "Exponential decay",
 187	    "description": "Change the rate to recompute the curve locally.",
 188	    "parameters": [
 189	      { "id": "rate", "label": "Decay rate", "min": 0.1, "max": 3,
 190	        "step": 0.1, "value": 1, "unit": "s⁻¹" }
 191	    ],
 192	    "plot": {
 193	      "x": { "id": "t", "label": "Time (s)", "min": 0, "max": 10, "samples": 160 },
 194	      "y_label": "Amplitude",
 195	      "series": [
 196	        { "label": "x(t)", "expression": "exp(-rate*t)" }
 197	      ]
 198	    },
 199	    "metrics": [
 200	      { "label": "Half-life", "expression": "ln(2)/rate", "unit": " s", "precision": 2 }
 201	    ]
 202	  }
 203	}
 204	```
 205	
 206	The web Surface evaluates expressions and updates the plot and metrics locally as
 207	controls move. A committed slider or number-input change emits:
 208	
 209	```json
 210	{
 211	  "type": "parameters_changed",
 212	  "payload": {
 213	    "parameters": { "rate": 1.4 },
 214	    "changed": { "id": "rate", "value": 1.4 }
 215	  }
 216	}
 217	```
 218	
 219	Expression support is deliberately bounded: numeric literals, named variables,
 220	parentheses, unary `+`/`-`, operators `+ - * / ^`, constants `pi`/`e`, and
 221	`sin`, `cos`, `tan`, `exp`, `ln`/`log`, `sqrt`, `abs`, `min`, and `max`.
 222	Limits are 12 parameters, 6 series, 512 samples, and 512 characters per
 223	expression. Invalid or non-finite work renders an inline error instead of plot
 224	geometry. This kind is currently interactive on the Leptos web/PWA/extension
 225	surface; other clients may project a fallback. It does not execute tools or
 226	external actions.
 227	
 228	#### `timeline`
 229	
 230	```json
 231	{ "id": "t1", "kind": "timeline",
 232	  "props": { "steps": [ { "label": "Plan", "status": "done", "detail": "..." },
 233	                        { "label": "Build", "status": "active" },
 234	                        { "label": "Ship", "status": "pending" } ] } }
 235	```
  60	Statuses: `done`, `active`, `pending`, `error`.
  61	
  62	### `interactive_plot` — locally explorable numeric relationships
  63	
  64	Use when users should change bounded numeric parameters and immediately see the
  65	resulting curve or derived metrics. Use `chart` instead for display-only data.
  66	The Surface evaluates the declared math locally; do not use this component to
  67	execute tools or external actions.
  68	
  69	```json
  70	{
  71	  "id": "decay-lab",
  72	  "kind": "interactive_plot",
  73	  "props": {
  74	    "title": "Exponential decay",
  75	    "parameters": [
  76	      { "id": "rate", "label": "Decay rate", "min": 0.1, "max": 3,
  77	        "step": 0.1, "value": 1, "unit": "s⁻¹" }
  78	    ],
  79	    "plot": {
  80	      "x": { "id": "t", "label": "Time", "min": 0, "max": 10, "samples": 160 },
  81	      "y_label": "Amplitude",
  82	      "series": [{ "label": "x(t)", "expression": "exp(-rate*t)" }]
  83	    },
  84	    "metrics": [
  85	      { "label": "Half-life", "expression": "ln(2)/rate", "unit": " s", "precision": 2 }
  86	    ]
  87	  }
  88	}
  89	```
  90	
  91	Expressions may use numeric literals, parameter ids, the x-axis id, `pi`, `e`,
  92	`+ - * / ^`, parentheses, and `sin`, `cos`, `tan`, `exp`, `ln`/`log`, `sqrt`,
  93	`abs`, `min`, and `max`. Limits: 12 parameters, 6 series, 512 samples, and 512
  94	characters per expression. A committed control change emits
  95	`parameters_changed` with the complete parameter map and the changed id/value.
  96	Use `component_wait` only when the running turn truly needs that committed
  97	choice; local preview does not require an agent round trip.
