  65	        "Mount or update a rich, interactive UI component in the client surface. \
  66	         On the web surface these render as live HTML — USE THEM LIBERALLY instead of \
  67	         hand-typing markdown for anything structured. `id` is an agent-chosen opaque \
  68	         string scoped to the session; reuse the same id with replace:true to update a \
  69	         component in place (e.g. advance a progress bar, flip a timeline step to done).\n\
  70	         \
  71	         WHEN TO REACH FOR WHICH KIND:\n\
  72	         • Rows/columns of data → 'table' (NEVER markdown pipe tables).\n\
  73	         • Task/status board → 'kanban'. Collecting input → 'form' (then component_wait).\n\
  74	         • A running task → 'progress'. A multi-step plan → 'timeline'.\n\
  75	         • KPIs / metrics (views, plays, saves) → 'stat'. Numeric series to visualize → 'chart'.\n\
  76	         • A graph users should explore by changing numeric parameters → 'interactive_plot'.\n\
  77	         • Project structure / file list → 'file_tree'. Showing code edits → 'diff'.\n\
  78	         • A code snippet to copy → 'code'. An important note/warning → 'callout'.\n\
  79	         • Images / screenshots / generated art → 'gallery'. A yes/no before something \
  80	         destructive → 'confirm' (then component_wait for the answer).\n\
  81	         • Anything geographic — locations, routes, where creators/streams/markets are → \
  82	         'map' (a live, pannable Google Map). Far better than describing coordinates in text.\n\
  83	         • A video to watch inline — a TikTok/Reel/YouTube link, or a direct video file → \
  84	         'video' (embeds and plays in the chat). Use for campaign clips, sound previews, references.\n\
  85	         • Several of the above at once → 'dashboard'. Long prose → 'markdown' (or plain text).\n\
  86	         \
  87	         PROPS SCHEMA BY KIND (props must match exactly):\n\
  88	         • table — { columns: [\"Name\",\"Status\"], rows: [[\"Fix login\",\"open\"],[\"Add tests\",\"done\"]] }. Emits row_clicked { row_index }.\n\
  89	         • kanban — { columns: [{id,title}], cards: [{id, column, title, description?}] }. Emits card_clicked.\n\
  90	         • form — { title, fields: [{name, label, type, required?, options?}], submit_label? }. type is text|textarea|select|number. Emits form_submit { <name>: value }.\n\
  91	         • progress — { label, value, max, indeterminate? }. value/max numbers (0.6/1.0). Display only.\n\
  92	         • markdown — { content: \"## md\" }. Rich prose; supports tables, bold, lists.\n\
  93	         • dashboard — { children: [{ id, width, kind?, props? }] }. Grid; width is fr units; inline kind+props renders that component in the cell.\n\
  94	         • chart — { title?, type: \"bar\"|\"line\", series: [{label, value}] }. value is numeric. Display only.\n\
  95	         • interactive_plot — { title?, description?, parameters: [{id,label?,min,max,step?,value,unit?}], plot: {x:{id?,label?,min,max,samples?}, y_label?, series:[{label,expression}]}, metrics?:[{label,expression,unit?,precision?}] }. Expressions use bounded arithmetic/functions; controls recompute locally and emit parameters_changed on commit.\n\
  96	         • timeline — { steps: [{label, status: \"done\"|\"active\"|\"pending\"|\"error\", detail?}] }. Re-render with replace:true to advance.\n\
  97	         • stat — { stats: [{label, value, delta?, trend: \"up\"|\"down\"|\"flat\"}] }. value is string or number.\n\
  98	         • file_tree — { root?, entries: [{name, type: \"file\"|\"dir\", path?, children?}] }. Dirs nest via children. Files emit file_clicked { path }.\n\
  99	         • diff — { filename?, lines: [{kind: \"add\"|\"del\"|\"ctx\", text}] }  OR  { filename?, unified: \"+new\\n-old\" }.\n\
 100	         • code — { language?, filename?, code }. Renders a copy-able code block.\n\
 101	         • callout — { variant: \"info\"|\"success\"|\"warn\"|\"error\", title?, body? }. body supports markdown.\n\
 102	         • gallery — { images: [{src, caption?}] }. src is a URL or data: URI.\n\
 103	         • confirm — { title, body?, confirm_label?, cancel_label?, variant? }. Emits confirm_response { confirmed: bool }.\n\
 104	         • map — { center: {lat, lng}, zoom?, markers?: [{lat, lng, title?, label?}], fit_markers? }. \
 105	         Live Google Map. `zoom` 1–20 (default ~10); `fit_markers:true` auto-frames all markers. \
 106	         Emits marker_clicked { index, title }.\n\
 107	         • video — { url, title?, autoplay?, start? }. `url` is a TikTok / Instagram Reel / \
 108	         YouTube / Vimeo link OR a direct .mp4/.webm/.m3u8 URL — the surface picks the right \
 109	         embed automatically. `start` is seconds offset (YouTube/file). Display only.\n\
 110	         \
 111	         Set replace:true to overwrite an existing component with the same id. \
 112	         Full reference: docs/AGENT_RENDER_PROTOCOL.md."
 113	    }
